## SECTION 4: DETAILED SCREEN-BY-SCREEN SPECIFICATION (F01 – F24)

### F01 — Owner Gate
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S01 / tour S01 / view keypad`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/components/BootLoader.tsx:85`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Identify owner-entry state before entering the spatial workspace with hardware-verified token validation.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: Single centered column. Keypad targets strictly >= 44x44px. Error feedback area reserved above entry action without causing layout shifts.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: Centered compact floating glass card (Void Black rgba(20,38,50,0.88), blur(20px), 1px hairline border). Never enlarge keypad merely to fill tablet viewport.
- **Visible Hierarchy:** Original NOJARA identity lockup (BrandLockup.tsx intrinsic aspect) / Four-position pin field / 3x4 Frosted numeric keypad / Dynamic error toast / Biometric bypass action.
- **Primary Interaction & Flow:** Complete 4-pin or biometric owner entry; smoothly transition to BootLoader (F02) with 320ms ease-out.
- **Required Lifecycle States:** Empty, partial input (1-3 dots), invalid input (shake animation + #E5484D glow), corrected input, authorized entry, keyboard focus.
- **Material Risk & Contract Conflict Resolution:** Client-side gate was previously treated as mock authentication. Must bind to verifiable auth token with secure session persistence.
- **Strict Acceptance Gate:** Zero brand substitution or distortion; no clipped copy or focus trap; hit targets >= 44x44px; bypass controls independently verifiable.

### F02 — Loading Sequence & Word-Sync Loader
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S02 / tour S01 / view loader`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/components/BootLoader.tsx:250`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Explain real spatial asset hydration and readiness without artificial delay, featuring audio-synced word-by-word motion typography.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: Stacked progress bar with auto-wrapping status text. Reserve status width and allow text to grow vertically without glyph collisions.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: Four loading milestones rendered at optimal reading width (max 480px). Align status indicators consistently with live percentage telemetry.
- **Visible Hierarchy:** NOJARA brand lockup & elapsed timer / Linear progress bar (#4C8DFF fill) / Staggered word-by-word animated phrase / Four real hydration items & statuses.
- **Primary Interaction & Flow:** Enter universe automatically when WebGL, shaders, and initial records are hydrated; allow explicit retry on failure; skip disabled unless QA mode.
- **Required Lifecycle States:** Hydration pending, shader compile, asset loading, ready, failed retry, reduced motion (instant fade), normal completion.
- **Material Risk & Contract Conflict Resolution:** Previous loader used artificial elapsed time intervals. Updated implementation must bind directly to real Three.js WebGL compile and data hydration promises.
- **Strict Acceptance Gate:** Record every asset load frame; no fake completion ticks; word reveals synchronized mathematically to audio timestamp (40ms stagger, blur(4px) -> 0).

### F03 — HQ Universe and Arrival
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S03 / tour S02 / view hq`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/components/CosmographCanvas.tsx:2397 & src/three/sphereNetwork.ts`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Establish the continuous primary spatial cosmic stage and the studio's operational station clusters in deep space.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: Dominant central HQ sphere framed within computed sceneSafeRect. Single bottom sheet dock with 72px peek and 264px default height.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: Reframed cosmic stage beside responsive 304px inspector panel. Generous negative space preserving orbital particle parallax.
- **Visible Hierarchy:** Transmissive HQ Sphere 01 ([0,0,0], r=6.2u) & internal 6,400-star spiral galaxy / Orbiting project & station nodes / Global header / Floating Voice Dock.
- **Primary Interaction & Flow:** Pinch-zoom down to 20% scale, orbit via spring-damper physics, tap sphere or station node to focus camera with continuous interpolation.
- **Required Lifecycle States:** Entrance flight, resting idle orbit, node hover highlight, selected node focus, interrupted flight, 20% zoom overview, reduced graphics fallback.
- **Material Risk & Contract Conflict Resolution:** Older screenshots showed crowded metallic spheres and opaque video textures on HQ. Latest update strictly locks Sphere 01 to MeshPhysicalMaterial (transmission 0.92, roughness 0.05, depthWrite false, map: null).
- **Strict Acceptance Gate:** Zero camera resets on node focus; internal galaxy completely visible without reflection clipping; continuous spring-damper physics with collision avoidance down to 20% scale.

### F04 — CDE Universe and Dimensions
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S04 / tour S17 / view cde`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/components/CosmographCanvas.tsx:2446 & src/three/sphereNetwork.ts`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Explore the four source-defined Culture and Design Engineering dimensions within the unified spatial stage.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: Focuses one CDE dimension at a time with concise title and swipe gestures; preserves full 4-dimension carousel access.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: Flanking 304px dimension inspector beside amber-crystal CDE Sphere 02 ([38,4,-22], r=6.2u).
- **Visible Hierarchy:** Amber-crystal CDE Sphere 02 / Four dimension nodes (Strategy, Production, Talent & Culture, Media Technology) / Subdomain cards / Contextual narrative.
- **Primary Interaction & Flow:** Select dimension to trigger camera flight; tap linked project chip to transition directly into Project Workspace (F07).
- **Required Lifecycle States:** Dimension idle, dimension focused, subdomain selected, project camera travel, return to CDE core, media decode error.
- **Material Risk & Contract Conflict Resolution:** App previously defaulted CDE to cobalt-glass. Schema locks CDE to amber-crystal with distinct refractive index and dedicated station routes.
- **Strict Acceptance Gate:** Independent verification of Strategy, Production, Talent, and Media Technology IDs/colors; no camera teleportation; seamless bookmark return to HQ.

### F05 — Responsive Panel Workspace
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S05 / tour Several / view pockets`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/gui/layoutEngine.ts:70 & src/components/PanelsOverlay.tsx`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Provide floating, modular workspace panels around a clear spatial center without visual bleeding or screen clutter.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: One contextual bottom sheet with tab bar (peek 72px, default 264px, expanded 480px) occupying safe rect without covering top brand lockup.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: Single 304px side inspector in portrait; dual 288px flanking inspectors in landscape (1180x820) wrapped in CSS 3D perspective.
- **Visible Hierarchy:** Measured sceneSafeRect clear zone / Flanking floating glass cards / Tab strip / Expand-collapse triggers / Voice Dock.
- **Primary Interaction & Flow:** Open, minimize to floating pill, restore, and close panels while preserving scroll position, active tab, and uncommitted form drafts.
- **Required Lifecycle States:** Zero panels (pure 3D stage), single panel, multi-tabbed panel, expanded sheet, keyboard open, restored draft state.
- **Material Risk & Contract Conflict Resolution:** Older builds suffered from unmounted v0.2 fallback DOM elements causing overlapping cards. Replaced by computeGuiLayout single-active-surface rule.
- **Strict Acceptance Gate:** Zero critical bounding-box overlap; 100% preservation of draft/scroll state on minimize/restore; full compliance with 20px blur and 1px hairline border.

### F06 — Portfolio Browser
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S06 / tour S04 / view portfolio`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/components/WireframesV11Panels.tsx:562`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Filter, search, and navigate live studio projects with truthful status badges and direct workspace transition.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: Vertically scrollable single-column card list inside bottom sheet. Horizontally scrollable filter pills with 44px hit targets.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: Structured 304px inspector list beside the 3D cosmic stage; active project highlights linked node in WebGL.
- **Visible Hierarchy:** Portfolio header & live project count / Filter pills (All, Active, Waiting on 39, Blocked) / Project card list with KPI badges / Open workspace CTA.
- **Primary Interaction & Flow:** Tap filter chip to filter in <=16ms; tap project card to initiate smooth camera flight to project station node and open F07.
- **Required Lifecycle States:** All projects, filtered subset, empty search result, project selected, stale snapshot warning, data loading, source error.
- **Material Risk & Contract Conflict Resolution:** Seeded 17-project mock data previously displayed fake live metrics. Schema mandates explicit snapshot/sample provenance labels.
- **Strict Acceptance Gate:** Every displayed project ID routes to valid project workspace; no forced detour through HQ; status colors match schema tokens.

### F07 — Project Workspace & Deep Inspector
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S07 / tour S05 / view project-detail`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/components/WireframesV11Panels.tsx:671`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Provide deep operational execution across nine functional tabs for a single verified studio project.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: Horizontally scrolling tab row with active indicator. Single responsive content card with vertical scroll and collapsible header.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: High-density 328px inspector card featuring CSS 3D perspective tilt (rotateX(12deg) rotateY(-8deg)) and negative space padding (24px).
- **Visible Hierarchy:** Project identity, provenance badge & client logo / 9 Workspace Tabs (Overview, Plan, Tasks, People, Files, Media, Budget, Timeline, Decisions) / KPI grid / Action dock.
- **Primary Interaction & Flow:** Switch tabs with zero lag; edit task or decision inline; tap media thumbnail to launch Media Showcase Modal (F15).
- **Required Lifecycle States:** Overview active, tasks tab, media reel, budget review, decision pending, draft edit, approval needed, camera follow.
- **Material Risk & Contract Conflict Resolution:** Hardcoded financial and budget numbers previously existed in templates. Now requires verified source provenance or explicit 'sample' disclaimer.
- **Strict Acceptance Gate:** Selected project ID and active tab persist across 3D camera orbits, minimize/restore cycles, and modal dismissals.

### F08 — Task Board and Task Detail
- **Registry Binding:** `Catalog S08 / tour S06 / view tasks`
- **Source Code Anchor:** `src/components/WireframesV11Panels.tsx:1015`
- **Architectural Purpose:** Track operational tasks across 4 workflow stages with persistent state verification and owner assignment.
- **Composition & Ergonomics:**
  - **Phone (390×844):** 390 x 844: Segmented status control (To Do, Doing, Waiting, Done) with vertical card stack; tap card opens full-sheet editor.
  - **iPad (820×1180):** 820 x 1180: Four-column Kanban board with readable 240px columns and smooth drag-and-drop or tap-to-move actions.
- **Visible Hierarchy:** Board header with filter & search / 4 Kanban columns / Task card (Title, assignee avatar, due date, status pill) / Task detail flyout.
